# Banter in Foxwillow and the Fields of the Crow (story/banter.gd plays this file only where a place's region is foxwillow): one exchange between two or three companions about what is in
# front of them in one place, gated on that place (`at:`) and on the story's state so a remark never runs ahead of the chapter. Played now and then on entering
# an area, once each; an exchange nobody present can speak comes out empty and is skipped.
# Drafted by Gemini (docs/plans/gemini_companions/), edited; every edit is listed in the README there. Lines are unvoiced until the voice lane reads them.


~ foxwillow_01_rook_cordelia
if name:rook_coldwake and name:cordelia_skein and at:foxwillow and not flag.fw_brawl_a_done
interject name:rook_coldwake: That windmill on the bluff is a wheel of fire, Cordelia, and the town pump is sitting right in Magpie Square doing nothing at all.
interject name:cordelia_skein: The smoke from that burning hay stook has a fascinating ratio of roasted gourd and char, darling. My six eyes can barely calibrate for the glare.
interject name:rook_coldwake: You have pumpkin-headed brawlers round the stone flock of magpies, and corn past the east fields grown three yards past zoning regulation.
interject name:cordelia_skein: You have also forgotten to inhale the ash for four minutes, Rook, though I suppose it spares your lungs the assay.
interject name:rook_coldwake: Right you are. There is a sigh for the shift log, though it tastes mostly of burnt squash.
endif
-> END

~ foxwillow_02_silas_tobin
if name:silas_vane and name:tobin_hayward and at:foxwillow and flag.fw_brawl_c_done and not flag.raum_slain
interject name:silas_vane: Three bouts cleared in Magpie Square, Tobin, and that field scarecrow in the bonnet folded the second the pitchfork hit the cobbles.
interject name:tobin_hayward: Do not gloat over shoddy stitch-work, Silas, and step round that pumpkin head at the pump before a stray ember catches my hem.
interject name:silas_vane: Easy, friend, I have my censer swinging to cut the reek off the butcher's pens, and there is not a live spark near William's cart.
interject name:tobin_hayward: Someone stuffed these folk with dry haulm and set them swinging against their own neighbours. You can still smell the tallow on the twine.
interject name:silas_vane: Bad hand dealt from a marked shoe, Tobin, and whoever is banking this game out past the east fields still owes the square a tab.
endif
-> END

~ fw_windmill_03_delphine_lucan
if name:delphine_ravelle and name:lucan_houndstooth and at:fw_windmill and not flag.fw_mill_done
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Look at that great cog grinding away overhead, Lucan, it sounds like stage machinery cranked by a stagehand with a grudge.
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: Hush by my boots, Barnaby, that is only timber groaning above the stair to the upper floor, not thunder. Keep behind me, if you please, Delphine.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Your Foolishness is pulling faces at the flour dust, and when he stops making puns about the billing, I start minding my seams.
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: The spoor on these steps is all charred straw and scorched grease, and poor Liza Sawyer looks half-choked by the draught.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Then let us climb before the roof comes down on the house. I refuse to be buried in meal like a penny sack.
endif
-> END

~ fw_store_04_tobin_delphine
if name:tobin_hayward and name:delphine_ravelle and at:fw_store and not flag.raum_slain
interject name:tobin_hayward: Back from that burning rubble, Delphine, two paces back. My mice are scrambling under my collar and the heat is blistering the paint on the shelves of staples.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Mind the seams, darling, I am felt and sawdust under the velvet, and I have no wish to go up like a cheap curtain either.
interject name:tobin_hayward: Look there in the cinders, just a banjo's neck left whole while the flour tins split at the solder.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Someone tuned it for the last number and left it when the roof fell in. Even my patron does not have a joke for a snapped string.
interject name:tobin_hayward: Come away from the embers and let me check your cuff for cinders. One scorched thread and the whole sleeve unravels.
endif
-> END

~ fw_library_05_cordelia_tobin
if name:cordelia_skein and name:tobin_hayward and at:fw_library and not flag.fw_librarian_done
interject name:cordelia_skein: Observe the tall stacks of books, Tobin, arranged with an almost pathological disregard for dry ventilation. The binding glue has soured to a fascinating viscosity.
interject name:tobin_hayward: That is damp-rot in the rag paper, Cordelia, and old mildew creeping up the spine-stitching like canker in an apple loft.
interject name:cordelia_skein: Agnes Fennel appears quite absorbed in her catalogue, darling, though her pulse from across the aisle is remarkably brisk for a parish clerk.
interject name:tobin_hayward: A good ledger ought to smell of linseed and dry flax, not cold tallow and shut windows. Keep your silk notes clear of the shelves.
interject name:cordelia_skein: Please, my crimson thread dissolves cleanly on the air. I would never leave an unindexed stain in another woman's collection.
endif
-> END

~ fw_circle_06_lucan_tobin
if name:lucan_houndstooth and name:tobin_hayward and at:fw_circle and not flag.raum_slain
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: Good heavens, Tobin, every stalk in this crop circle is flattened to the millimetre, yet the posture of the figure in the centre is deeply unsettling.
interject name:tobin_hayward: Good soil, bad seed, Lucan, and a taproot fed on something foul. You could not bend haulm this thick with a heavy roller.
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: Barnaby just gave a sharp yip by my heel, and I assure you there is no dropped kettle corn in this clearing. The air tastes of cold iron and bruised husk.
interject name:tobin_hayward: That is Virgil standing in the flattened rows, and the twine at his joints was never tied by a farmhand's thumb.
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: I would award the geometry an eight out of ten for symmetry, my friend, if my hackles would only lie flat enough to write it down.
endif
-> END

~ fw_maze_j1_07_silas_delphine
if name:silas_vane and name:delphine_ravelle and at:fw_maze_j1 and not flag.raum_slain
interject name:silas_vane: Hear the crows' calls rattling off the leaves, Delphine? Every bird in this clearing is cawing on the off-beat like a rigged wheel.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: They are heckling from the cheap seats, and Your Foolishness is mimicking them in my ear until my button eye aches.
interject name:silas_vane: Tell's in the twitch, and the wind coming through these stalks is whistling straight across my ribs like a cold blade.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Your little shadow is lagging a full half-step behind your heels, Silas, and it keeps looking up at the tassels.
interject name:silas_vane: Let it look. As long as I can still shuffle bone cards with one hand, the house has not closed the walls on us yet.
endif
-> END

~ foxwillow_08_silas_lucan
if name:silas_vane and name:lucan_houndstooth and at:foxwillow and flag.raum_slain
interject name:silas_vane: Raum is down for the count, Lucan, the fires are dying down to grey ash, and I just chalked one very large tally mark inside my ribs.
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: A prime specimen of rural malice, Silas, though I am far happier seeing the townsfolk breathing clean air by the north lanes.
interject name:silas_vane: Even the smoke drifting over the rooftops smells like plain wet timber again instead of a rigged table.
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: Some of the townsfolk are still staring toward the east fields as if the stalks might march back into the schoolyard. It takes a long while for a parish to unlearn the dark.
interject name:silas_vane: Tell Barnaby he can stop shaking behind your boots, friend. The fire on the mill bluff has cashed in its chips.
endif
-> END
